    <item>
      <title>Zangezi</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/zangezi/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 13 Nov 2021 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/zangezi/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;&amp;ldquo;Zangezi is a sextet accompanied by a “visual artist&amp;rdquo; and a &amp;ldquo;sound designer&amp;rdquo; that strives for an artificial but organic sound production aesthetic.&amp;quot; As the visual artist in this sextet, I composed the live-visuals in this piece along with camera support from Hoi Man. Much of the visuals were created with live-camera input along with elements made using footage filmed the day before during our rehearsals. In this work, the visuals mainly played with temporality and multiplicity of the image.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
    <item>
      <title>Rickey Mouse saga</title>
      <link>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/rickey-mouse/</link>
      <pubDate>Sat, 19 Dec 2020 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
      
      <guid>http://localhost:1313/projects/live/rickey-mouse/</guid>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Rickey Mouse Fun House was a project led by Finnish artist, Pasi Mäkelä. I initially joined this constellation in the role of support camera and video editor during their first performance which was &lt;a
  href=&#34;https://youtu.be/3J7kacIyDzE&#34;
    target=&#34;_blank&#34;
  &gt;live streamed from Punctum&lt;/a&gt; (Prague, CZ) in December 2020. From the following year, I began creating the live-visuals we would use in the show. Spiritually and formally rooted in experiment and play, this project was genuinely &lt;em&gt;fun&lt;/em&gt; to be a part of. I was able to come in and develop all the live-camera things I wanted to play with, while also learning how these phenomenal musicians improvised together using specific counting systems and timing to enhance the audience&amp;rsquo;s listening experience as well as their own experiences of playing live music. I developed my practise of working with the simplicity of OBS Studio and pushing its limits by building visuals using chroma/luma keying, layering, collaging, screen inputs, source repetition, multiple camera inputs and multiple projections.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
      
    </item>
    
